<title>UK: Brake Brothers makes French acquisition.</title>
<headline>Brake Brothers makes French acquisition.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Foods manfacturer Brake Brothers Plc on Thursday said it had entered into an agreement to acquire, for an undisclosed sum, D.R.V. SA (Vermes) a leading supplier of frozen an chilled foods to caterers in South West France.</p>
<p>Privately owned Vermes which has net tangile assets of 3.2 million stg, reported pre-tax profits in the year to 31 December 1995 of 700,000 stg on turnover of around 27 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
